<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">José Antonio Aguirre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1904">1904</a>–<a href="/years/1960">1960</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as José Antonio Aguirre y Lecube</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">José Antonio Aguirre was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basque-nationalist-party">Basque Nationalist Party</a> politician and former footballer who became the first lehendakari, or president, of the autonomous Basque government. He took his oath under the oak of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guernica">Guernica</a> on 7 October 1936, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-civil-war">Spanish Civil War</a>. After Francoist forces took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bilbao">Bilbao</a> in 1937 he led the Basque government in exile until his death.</p></div>
